+## 2. Candidates (≤ 8 concrete simplifications/repeals)
+
+Presented as questions ("asking, not proposing bills" — scope policy, not a compliance adjudication).
+
+### C1 — Act 10 instrument + baseline + 24h comparative report — REPEAL (redundant with Act 31 §8 + Act 32 Stats Bureau)
+- **Target text:** "The Research Office shall maintain a durable per-sitting record containing: seats intervened, ballots cast, bills proposed/passed, mandates created/closed, wall-clock duration, and a host resource sample (RAM used, CPU load) at sitting start. The resource sample must include cgroup memory metrics — memory.current, memory.max, and memory.events (max-limit hits and OOM kills) — not only host-level free" (LAWS.md:104); "The Research Office shall publish a baseline of the pre-change design (records/research/2026-10-14-initial-sitting-baseline.md) and, after a 24-hour measurement window under event-driven sittings, a comparative report..." (LAWS.md:106); event-driven sittings (LAWS.md:105).
+- **Simplified form:** Remove Act 10 §1–§2 as law text; the standing measurement channel is Act 31 §8's daily sitting (LAWS.md:485) + Act 32 Stats Bureau §1 (LAWS.md:498–507, "Existing collectors are inputs, not proof") + Act 30 §7 digest (LAWS.md:473).
+- **Benefit claim + evidence:** *Unmeasured post-sunset.* Measured during renewal window: load 8.99 → 2.74–5.30, seat RSS ~5,300 → 1,511–4,389 MB (ACT10-RENEWAL-ASSESSMENT.md:9–17) — renewal window lapsed (LAWS.md:101/108; automatic sunset on OOM, LAWS.md:102–103). Benefit claim: weak.
+- **Cost of change:** Very low (text deletion). Regression risk: if Act 31 §8 delivery thins, observability shrinks — mitigated by Act 32 Stats Bureau §1 (independent, source-dependence-checked, LAWS.md:498–507).
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 18 §5 board trail — unaffected; Act 16 §2 schedule — unaffected; Act 21/28 — unaffected; Act 23 §4.1 — unaffected.
+- **Minimal experiment:** Re-measure under Act 31 §8 law: one sitting window comparing cgroup `memory.current`/`memory.max`/`memory.events` + outcomes (ballots/bills/deliverables) against ACT10-CGROUP-METRICS-2026-10-15.md; renew/repeat only if measured improvement holds.
+
+### C2 — Act 11 — REPEAL-as-reorganize (near-duplicate of Act 4 §5)
+- **Target text:** Act 11 (LAWS.md:110–116) vs Act 4 §5 (LAWS.md:34–38).
+- **Simplified form:** Fold Act 11 §3's suspension trigger ("suspends the non-compliant agent's credentials within one sitting cycle and escalates to the Founder") into an amendment of Act 4 §34–38 by the same legalizing vote (Act 6.3); REPEAL Act 11 otherwise.
+- **Benefit:** ~2/3 of Act 11 text removed; audit readability lower. Weak.
+- **Cost:** Near-zero. Risk: compliance-enforcement gap if the amendment is not adopted; mitigated by explicit condition: amendment filed before Act 11 removal, not silent.
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 4 §5 keeps all operational checks (LAWS.md:34–38); Act 21/28 — unaffected.
+- **Minimal experiment:** Diff LAWS.md:34–38 vs LAWS.md:110–116; propose REPEAL Act 11 + amendment in one Act 6.3 filing with diff as evidence (design).
+
+### C3 — Act 20 (Detector Calibration) — consolidate 7 clauses to core 4 (Keep)
+- **Target text:** LAWS.md:188–194 (§1 archive ≥8; §2 replay harness; §3 report; §4 held-out; §5 drift; §6 maintenance; §7 falsifiers).
+- **Simplified form:** Keep §1, §3, §4, §7 (fold §5 alarm semantics into Act 33 meter + §7 text).
+- **Benefit:** Predicted overhead reduction in Act 20 instrumentation for permanent instruments (Act 20 covers trials? no — Act 20's calculus is for the trial regime in fact: Act 20 §8 says P1–P5 are carried into the ledger (LAWS.md:214); Act 20 §4 held-out for 25%+2 by Clerk — is this the same regime as Act 33 §1/§4LAWS.md:767? — measure-benefit unmeasured.)
+- **Cost:** High; regression risk: permanent instruments may lose Act 20-era quality experience.
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 33 unchanged; Act 22 §7 (LAWS.md:214) carried into ledger — unchanged; Act 32 §9C gate (LAWS.md:657–663) — unchanged.
+- **Minimal experiment:** Pilot: Act 33 meter under 4-core vs 7-clause rule for known-answer case set (10 cases/3 instruments, LAWS.md:188); compare telemetry overhead, TP/FP, and whether recorded readings changed (falsifier: TP<1.0, FP>0 — LAWS.md:194).
+
+### C4 — Act 18 automation of terminal-stage postings
+- **Target text:** LAWS.md:169–177 + `board-trail-check.sh:2–17`.
+- **Simplified form:** Extend `board-trail-check.sh`/`board-trail-refresh.sh` (inventory) to post, per issue with a derived terminal state and no stage marker, one concise terminal transition line (deterministic stage = the derived terminal state).
+- **Benefit:** Predicted attention saving; not measured.
+- **Cost:** Medium; new law (Act 18.x) needed. Anti-chatter compliant: posts *terminal* transitions only (Act 18 §4: "Automated scheduler/agent status lines are not transitions" — transitions are fine).
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 18 §2 outcome invariant (LAWS.md:170) intent preserved; Act 18 §3–§6 unchanged; Act 16 §2 measurable via board-trail-check.
+- **Minimal experiment:** Run `board-trail-check.sh`; count issues with terminal state but no stage marker; if ≥20%, file C4-extension.
+
+### C5 — Act 30 §6 REPEAL (superseded by Act 31 §8) + Act 30 §5/§7 consolidation
+- **Target text:** LAWS.md:472–474 vs LAWS.md:485 ("Act 30 §6 is amended accordingly").
+- **Simplified form:** REPEAL Act 30 §6 (text ≡ Act 31 §8); consolidate Act 30 §5 + §7 into Act 30 §6 (daily sitting + summon + digest content).
+- **Benefit:** Text-level redundancy only; nothing predicted to move.
+- **Cost:** Near-zero.
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 31 §8 text unchanged; digest content preserved (no external dependency; Act 31 §8 amendment history at LAWS.md:485).
+- **Minimal experiment:** Legal diff: compare LAWS.md:472–474 vs LAWS.md:485 text-similarity; declare the REPEAL designed on this comparison (no execution per scope).
+
+### C6 — Consolidate the four standing "quality instrument" registers into the Act 30 §7 digest + suite bundle
+- **Target text:** LAWS.md:208–217 (Act 22 ledger); LAWS.md:612–637 (Act 32 §10 evaluation); LAWS.md:153–154 (Act 16 §3); LAWS.md:188–194 (Act 20 calibration).
+- **Simplified form:** One deterministic daily "measurement digest": columns for (a) Act 22 summary (registered count, coverage, Brier/log scores, discrimination, per-author), (b) Act 32 §10 office-activity fraction, (c) Act 16 §3 pre-registered criteria; published to Act 30 §7.
+- **Benefit:** Predicted ~10–30% overhead reduction; not disproven; depends on measurement (M17).
+- **Cost:** High; regression risk: each gate has independent value (Act 15 §2 measurement independence).
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 22 §1 (LAWS.md:209) still enforced; Act 16 §2 unchanged; Act 15 §2 unchanged; Act 32 §10 unchanged (access to Stat Bureau reports continues).
+- **Minimal experiment:** Census of standing-gate overhead: sum per-actor minutes per window across the four; if total < 5 min, retire candidate.
+
+### C7 — Act 33 hard-caps → daily-digest as secondary signal
+- **Target text:** Act 33 §4LAWS.md:771 (authorization+cancellation); Act 33 §3LAWS.md:769 (hard caps); Act 33 §5LAWS.md:773 (value gates).
+- **Simplified form:** Daily digest includes a row per Act 33 trial: current vs cap, days remaining, overrun flag — derived from `statistics-trial-meter.py` data (producer reads; digest consumes; I did not verify the consume step).
+- **Benefit:** Predicted marginal attention benefit (caps already exist per Act 33 §3).
+- **Cost:** Low.
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 33 unchanged.
+- **Minimal experiment:** Read `daily-digest.py` (inventory) — if it derives days-since-last-durable-result (required by Act 30 §7 wording, LAWS.md:473), C7 closes as "already implemented".
+
+### C8 — Act 31 §4 independent review → auto-approve for purely additive-records changes
+- **Target text:** Act 31 §4 (LAWS.md:480–481): "except additive records: changes that only add new files or append to existing files, all under records/, which cannot destroy evidence and land on a green suite without review."
+- **Simplified form:** Extend `review-delivery.sh`/`board-trail-check.sh`: additive-records diffs where board-trail-check is green (no Git-only gap, terminal marker present) auto-approve (recorded).
+- **Benefit:** Predicted ratio of approval-ready changes; ~20-30% of records-only changes (design: sample).
+- **Cost:** Medium; regression risk: Git-only-gap detection as measurement remains mandatory (Act 18 §2); classifier must be conservative (design).
+- **Invariant compatibility:** Act 31 §4 protected matters (LAWS.md:481): constitution/, law text, ballots — auto-approve only additive-records.
+- **Minimal experiment:** Diff last 30 days of additive records changes; count fraction where board-trail-check passes; compare vs non-additive pass rate; if ratio > 3:1, recommend.
