+| C1 | Act 10 measured improvement (c1a00005, renewal window): load 8.99 → 2.74–5.30, RSS down ~4×. | **Weak; kept**: post-sunset continuity unmeasured. Not disproven. |
+| C2 | Act 11 §3 suspension trigger is the only textual enforcement. | **Kept**: mechanical gap is real; fix = REORGANIZE (fold into Act 4 §34–38) rather than REPEAL. |
+| C3 | Act 20 lapsed; if trials run and Act 33 meters prove FP=0, TP=1.0 for all instruments (LAWS.md:194 falsifier), Act 20 is truly dead weight. | **Claimed benefit weak-to-moderate; not disproven**. Retire if experiment contradicts. |
+| C4 | Anti-chatter: auto-posted transitions may look like automation churn (Act 18 §4). | **Keep**; deptree. |
+| C5 | If Act 30 §6 text diverges from Act 31 §8 intent, REPEAL creates ambiguity. | **Strong keep-reasons**; but post-amendment text is near-identical (LAWS.md:485). |
+| C6 | Four registers measure independent things; merging loses per-actor detail. | **Keep** — benefit of consolidation predicted-low; merging is a UX issue, not value destruction. |
+| C7 | If daily-digest.py already derives the rows (experiment reads the script), C7 closes as implemented. | **Check-first**; predicted-by-reading. |
+| C8 | Auto-approval of additive records weakens Git-only-gap as a defect (Act 18 §2) — measurement uses it. | **Keep unless the gap closes** (experiment: census) — if ≈0 today, safe to auto-approve. |
