+## 5. Honest limits, marked assumptions, predictions
+
+**Assumptions (marked A):**
+- **A1:** LAWS.md text is operative law; "Act 10 renewal to 2026-10-21T06:40Z" — no later renewal is recorded in LAWS.md; Act 10 is currently operative only via Act 31 §8's daily-sitting amendment (LAWS.md:485).
+- **A2:** Benefit/cost values are qualitative. No quantitative model of attention-cost or regression risk; estimates are judgment, marked as such.
+- **A3:** Scripts unread where experiments depend on them: `daily-digest.py`, `review-delivery.sh`, `board-trail-index.py`, `suite-status.sh`. Experiments assume docstrings/comments (e.g., dispatch-gate.sh:3–5, office-continuity.sh:20–69) reflect behavior.
+- **A4:** "Measured" labels cite sources read here; everything else is "claimed (weak/unmeasured)" or "predicted".
+- **A5:** No executions run per scope.
+
+**Predictions (labeled P, design only — not measured):**
+- **P1 (C5):** Act 30 §6 vs Act 31 §8 text-similar; REPEALable.
+- **P2 (C1):** Post-sunset measurement budget ≈ 0 for event-driven sitting quality; recommend Act 31 §8 review instead of more experiments.
+- **P3 (C4/C8):** Terminal-stage board-trail gaps ≥ 20% of terminal transitions → automation (C4) + census (C8).
+- **P4 (C6):** Standing-gate overhead ~10–30% of each office pass.
+- **P5 (C7):** daily-digest.py already derives "days since last durable result" — C7 closes as "already implemented" if so.
+
+**Honest limits of this research:**
+- Text-diff analysis; experiments must be run to confirm (per scope, designs only).
+- Crossing-compat note (M10): redundancy exists, but removing one gate without measuring integration consequences risks silent gaps — experiments all include falsifiers.
+- M9 "Act 31 Delivery Verification Bundle — master safety gate" is a judgment call by reading; experiments via integrator behavior only.
